Don't regenerate the ANTLR grammar at build time

BuildPyCommand unconditionally re-runs ANTLR via `java -jar ...` before
every build, even though the sdist already ships omegaconf/grammar/gen/
pre-generated for runtime 4.9.3 (the exact version this recipe depends
on, see python3-antlr4-runtime_4.9.3.bb). This Yocto build has no Java
toolchain, so do_compile fails with "No such file or directory: 'java'".

Since the shipped generated files already match the pinned runtime,
regenerating them is redundant here -- just build from what's shipped.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific: avoids a build-time Java dependency]

--- a/build_helpers/build_helpers.py
+++ b/build_helpers/build_helpers.py
@@ -55,9 +55,9 @@

 class BuildPyCommand(build_py.build_py):  # pragma: no cover
     def run(self) -> None:
-        if not self.dry_run:
-            self.run_command("clean")
-            run_antlr(self)
+        # Yocto: skip clean+run_antlr(java) here -- the sdist already ships
+        # the ANTLR grammar pre-generated for runtime 4.9.3, and this build
+        # has no Java toolchain to regenerate it.
         build_py.build_py.run(self)
